====================================================
JENKINS TMP ISSUE TROUBLESHOOTING GUIDE
====================================================

ISSUE:
----------------------------------------------------
Jenkins build failing with errors like:

java.io.IOException: No space left on device

OR

Failed to create temporary file

This happens when the /tmp directory becomes full.

====================================================
STEP 1: CHECK DISK SPACE
====================================================

Check overall disk usage:

sudo df -h

Check only /tmp:

df -h /tmp

Example Output:

Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use%
/dev/root        20G   20G     0 100%

If Available Space = 0, Jenkins may fail.

====================================================
STEP 2: CLEAN TEMP FILES
====================================================

Remove temporary files:

sudo rm -rf /tmp/*

Verify:

df -h /tmp

====================================================
STEP 3: CLEAN APT CACHE
====================================================

sudo apt clean

Verify disk space:

df -h

====================================================
STEP 4: CONFIGURE JENKINS TO USE /var/tmp
====================================================

Open Jenkins Service Configuration:

sudo systemctl edit jenkins

Add the following:

[Service]
Environment="JAVA_OPTS=-Djava.io.tmpdir=/var/tmp"

Save and Exit.

Nano Commands:

CTRL + O
ENTER
CTRL + X

====================================================
STEP 5: RELOAD SYSTEMD
====================================================

sudo systemctl daemon-reload

====================================================
STEP 6: RESTART JENKINS
====================================================

sudo systemctl restart jenkins

Check Status:

sudo systemctl status jenkins

Expected:

Active: active (running)

====================================================
STEP 7: VERIFY CONFIGURATION
====================================================

sudo systemctl cat jenkins

Expected Output:

[Service]
Environment="JAVA_OPTS=-Djava.io.tmpdir=/var/tmp"

====================================================
STEP 8: CHECK JENKINS LOGS
====================================================

Live Logs:

sudo journalctl -u jenkins -f

Last 100 Logs:

sudo journalctl -u jenkins -n 100

====================================================
STEP 9: CHECK /var/tmp SPACE
====================================================

df -h /var/tmp

Example:

Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use%
/dev/root        20G   10G   10G 50%

====================================================
STEP 10: DOCKER CLEANUP
====================================================

Remove Stopped Containers:

docker container prune -f

Remove Unused Images:

docker image prune -a -f

Remove Unused Volumes:

docker volume prune -f

Complete Docker Cleanup:

docker system prune -a -f

====================================================
USEFUL JENKINS COMMANDS
====================================================

Check Jenkins Status:

sudo systemctl status jenkins

Restart Jenkins:

sudo systemctl restart jenkins

Stop Jenkins:

sudo systemctl stop jenkins

Start Jenkins:

sudo systemctl start jenkins

View Service File:

sudo systemctl cat jenkins

====================================================
COMPLETE FIX COMMANDS
====================================================

df -h

sudo apt clean

sudo rm -rf /tmp/*

sudo systemctl edit jenkins

Add:

[Service]
Environment="JAVA_OPTS=-Djava.io.tmpdir=/var/tmp"

Save and Exit

sudo systemctl daemon-reload

sudo systemctl restart jenkins

sudo systemctl status jenkins

sudo systemctl cat jenkins

====================================================
ROOT CAUSE
====================================================

/tmp directory becomes full.

Jenkins cannot create temporary files.

Builds fail with:

- No space left on device
- Failed to create temporary file

====================================================
PERMANENT SOLUTION
====================================================

Configure Jenkins to use:

JAVA_OPTS=-Djava.io.tmpdir=/var/tmp

and periodically clean:

- /tmp
- APT Cache
- Docker Images
- Docker Containers
- Docker Volumes

